-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- Historic Fit & Proper declarations backfill.
--
-- Source: docs/Historic FPA Declarations/*.xlsx (17 previously-completed
-- Personal Questionnaires, captured outside this system before the Fit & Proper
-- Declaration form existed here). This migration creates:
--   1. One fp_individuals row per unique person (16 individuals).
--   2. One fp_assessments row per historic submission (17 — one person,
--      Randall Kyle, has two separate historic PQ submissions for two different roles).
--   3. Each assessment is pinned (form_template_id/form_version_id) to the Fit &
--      Proper Declaration form (form_type='fit_and_proper', service='declaration')
--      created earlier — NOT the older generic seed PQ form — so opening these
--      historic records renders the same 19-tab layout the data was captured
--      against. No form_responses row is created (it requires a NOT NULL real
--      user_id); PinnedPqForm already falls back to fp_assessments.declaration_data
--      directly when no form_responses row exists (see FitAndProperAssessmentDetail.tsx).
--
-- assessment_type is assigned pseudo-randomly among initial/renewal/change_of_role
-- per instruction — the source files don't indicate a specific initiation type.
-- licensee_id/role_id are left NULL — no attempt is made to match/create licensee
-- entities from the free-text "Name of Licensee(s)" field on PQ01.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- ── Individuals ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
